# Scene 3: model your world. The home page's six cards, then two of them live on /tour/: relations broken one way
# after another, and a state machine walked. Recorded against the landing branch's build served on 127.0.0.1:8765
# (README.md); Chromium, which paints while reel isn't the active app.
Import //reels/entities.reelpreset
Open http://127.0.0.1:8765/index.html#world

Output //.artifacts/reel/scenes/03-model.mp4
Set Browser chromium
Set Viewport 1440x1040
Set WaitTimeout 20s
Set ClickRipples on

Hide
Wait css:"#world .wcard"
Sleep 1500ms
Show
Say@over "One order is where it starts. The same rules reach across your model: relations, [time] time, state machines, [ops] what an operation may do, values, and [files] the files a model points at. [done]"
Wait [time]
Zoom css:"#world .wcard:nth-of-type(2)" 1.4x
Wait [ops]
Zoom off
Scroll down 5 css:"#world"
Zoom css:"#world .wcard:nth-of-type(4)" 1.3x
Wait [files]
Zoom css:"#world .wcard:nth-of-type(6)" 1.3x
Wait [done]
Zoom off
# A marker at the end of a long line is found before the line ends; hold for the rest of it.
Sleep 2s

Hide
Open http://127.0.0.1:8765/tour/index.html#relations
Wait css:"button[data-sc='dup']"
Sleep 1s
Show
Say "Think of it as a database model, and break it."
Say@over "A duplicate key, [dup] a reference to nothing, [ref] a cycle, [cyc] a chain of redirects. [chain]"
Wait [dup]
Click css:"button[data-sc='dup']"
Wait [ref]
Click css:"button[data-sc='ref']"
Wait [cyc]
Click css:"button[data-sc='cyc']"
Wait [chain]
Click css:"button[data-sc='chain']"
Say "Each one a named rule, with a failure that says which."

Hide
Open http://127.0.0.1:8765/tour/index.html#machines
Wait css:"#mc-step"
Sleep 1s
Show
Say@over "And a lifecycle, [walk] walked one legal move at a time, and drawn from the same definition, so the diagram in your docs can't drift."
Wait [walk]
Click css:"#mc-new"
Click css:"#mc-step"
Sleep 600ms
Click css:"#mc-step"
Sleep 600ms
Click css:"#mc-step"
Sleep 1500ms
